-- title:
--   Shared unweighted graph representation, paths, and call-cost specifications
-- statement:
--   This shared module defines a finite directed graph by adjacency lists on vertices 0,…,n−1. Parallel arcs count separately in m, the sum of row lengths; self-loops are allowed. It connects that graph to an allocated UnweightedGraph object with arrays of adjacency arrays and degrees. It defines edge-counted walks, reachability, shortest distance, mutual reachability, root permutations, and transposition preserving arc multiplicity. Caller-storage preservation includes all initially allocated sequences, objects, and collections, monotone allocation counters, nondecreasing graph_work, and unchanged other clocks. Freshness and distinctness predicates specify result allocation. The generated constructor semantics and public field interfaces are included. These are definitions, not proofs of traversal correctness.
